BackgroundRatesTest
└── refreshRates
    ├── given a cycle is already running
    │   └── it joins that cycle rather than starting a second
    ├── given the cached rates are still fresh
    │   ├── it does not fetch
    │   └── when the caller forces a refresh
    │       └── it fetches anyway
    ├── given the cached rates are stale
    │   ├── it waits a random moment before fetching
    │   ├── given nothing is cached at all
    │   │   └── it does not wait, because the user is watching
    │   ├── given a forced refresh joins a cycle already waiting
    │   │   ├── it leaves no timer behind
    │   │   └── it cuts the wait short
    │   ├── given an unforced refresh joins a cycle already waiting
    │   │   └── it leaves the wait in place
    │   ├── it reports that it is fetching
    │   └── it reports that it is waiting
    ├── given Nym is disabled
    │   ├── it fetches directly
    │   ├── it tells the provider which source the user chose
    │   ├── given the fetch succeeds
    │   │   └── it stores the rates
    │   ├── given the fetch fails
    │   │   └── it reports the provider errors
    │   └── given the provider reports a failure but returns rates anyway
    │       └── it stores nothing
    ├── given Nym is enabled
    │   ├── it never falls back to a direct fetch
    │   ├── it tells the provider the fetch is going through the mixnet
    │   ├── given the first attempt succeeds
    │   │   ├── it stores the rates
    │   │   ├── it clears any backoff
    │   │   └── it notes the success in the log
    │   ├── given the first attempt fails
    │   │   ├── it tears the connection down for a fresh gateway
    │   │   ├── it tries again
    │   │   └── it waits before churning to a new gateway
    │   ├── given every attempt fails
    │   │   ├── it backs off before the next cycle
    │   │   ├── it waits fifteen minutes before trying the mixnet again
    │   │   ├── it does not tear down a gateway it will not use
    │   │   ├── it reports the failure
    │   │   └── it narrates each attempt in the log
    │   ├── given the provider reports a failure but returns rates anyway
    │   │   └── it stores nothing
    │   ├── given the backoff window is still open
    │   │   ├── it skips the cycle entirely
    │   │   ├── it explains why the rate is not updating
    │   │   └── when the caller forces a refresh
    │   │       └── it fetches anyway
    │   └── given the backoff window has just expired
    │       └── it fetches again
    ├── given a fetch outlives the worker's idle timer
    │   ├── it keeps the worker alive
    │   └── given the browser cannot report platform info
    │       └── it keeps fetching anyway
    ├── given the fetch fails with no error to report
    │   └── it says so generically
    ├── given the fetch throws
    │   ├── it reports the error rather than rejecting
    │   └── given what was thrown is not an Error
    │       └── it still reports something readable
    └── storing rates
        ├── it merges over the existing cache
        ├── given some currencies fail the plausibility check
        │   ├── it keeps the ones that passed
        │   └── it names them in the log
        ├── given every currency passes the plausibility check
        │   └── it says nothing about rejections
        ├── given every currency fails the plausibility check
        │   ├── it stores nothing
        │   └── it reports the failure
        ├── given the held rate is unchanged
        │   ├── it is not rewritten
        │   └── it says nothing about a re-peg
        ├── given spot has left the band
        │   ├── it re-pegs
        │   └── it says how wide the band was
        └── it reports success
